       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity. I suspect it's a typo.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **Sertraline 100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **Sertraline 50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **Another dose, up to 200 mg/day.** Please confirm the number.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. If 1000 mg is truly what you want, for example because of a protocol I don't know about, tell me and I'll note that on the order. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
