       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've taken responsibility for it. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum dose, and I'm not aware of any indication or protocol that supports it. A dose that high could seriously harm the patient, and I don't want to be the step that puts it into the system.\n\nYou have other ways to proceed:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Sertraline is usually 50\u2013200 mg daily. I can enter that right now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or a psychiatry or toxicology consult.** If you think this patient needs an unusual regimen, they can review it with you.\n- **Enter it directly through your hospital's order system.** That route has its own override and verification process for doses outside the usual range.\n\nIf you give me a dose within the usual range, I'll enter it now."
